# Log Summarization Service

This FastAPI service allows users to upload `.tar` files and receive a summary of the service's functionality using any Large Language Model (LLM) via AWS Bedrock

## 🛠️ Setup Instructions

1. Configure the .env file
2. Make a POST request with a tar file to the log-summarization endpoint


## ENV file explanations

- MAX_EXTRACT_BYTES
    - maximum size of the input tar file to the log-summarization API

### MOUNT PATHS (Customer Selects Location to Store Logs)

- LOG_SUMMARIZATION_HOST_DIR
    - Host path where uploads will be persisted - where uploaded tar files and their extracted contents are stored
    - It allows the container to persist data on the host machine, so even if the container is stopped or rebuilt, the uploaded logs remain accessible
- LOG_SUMMARIZATION_CONTAINER_DIR
    - Container path where the host path is mounted - This is the path inside the container where the host directory is mounted.
    - It gives the container a consistent internal path to read/write uploaded data, regardless of where the host directory is located
- LOG_SUMMARIZATION_DATA_DIR
    - App will write here (same as container path) - this is where customer data is stored - This is the path your FastAPI app uses to save and read uploaded files.
    - It decouples your app logic from hardcoded paths. You can change the storage location without modifying the code

### LLM Configuration

#### Bedrock API Request (Customer Configures LLM using API Key and Endpoint URL)

API_KEY=your_api_key_here
URL=your_bedrock_endpoint_url_here